          "id": "d1fcfc736b5dd5ba346de750c27dd3419b89d513",
          "message": "perf(qwen4_exp): sequence-parallel HC residual streams for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next TP prefill (#2834)\n\n* perf(qwen4_exp): sequence-parallel HC residual streams for TP prefill\n\nUnder TP the 4-stream hyper-connection residual (grouped norm, the two\nlow-rank GEMMs, gated mean) is per-token and replicated, so every rank\nrepeated it on all tokens (~30% of TP4 prefill GPU time). For forwards with\n>= ATOM_QWEN4_EXP_SP_MIN_TOKENS tokens (default 1024, eager prefill only;\nnever under graph capture), keep the streams token-sharded after the PLE\nlayer: sub-layer inputs are all-gathered, sub-layer partial sums\nreduce-scattered (same bytes as the all-reduce they replace), and the HC\nwork is split TP ways.\n\nSharded layers skip mix_fused_quant: the FP8 attention-input projection\nquantizes the gathered BF16 rows itself, as the unsharded path already does\nabove HC_QUANT_ROWS_MAX rows.\n\n* fix(qwen4_exp): keep SP off when no layer follows PLE; CPU tests for the token sharding\n\nWith PLE on the last decoder layer the loop never sharded the streams, yet\nboth output paths still all-gathered them, returning tp x the rows. SP now\nstays off when sp_start_layer >= end_layer.\n\ntests/test_qwen4_exp_sequence_parallel.py runs _SequenceParallel and\nQwen4ExpModel.forward on simulated TP ranks (threads meeting in mocked\nall_gather / reduce_scatter_tensor): shard/gather round trips and\nreduce-scatter sums for even and uneven token counts, and a sharded forward\nagainst the unsharded one in both output modes, including PLE on the last\nlayer (fails without the fix).\n\n* perf(qwen4_exp): pad only the local rows in _SequenceParallel.shard\n\nFor token counts not divisible by TP, shard() padded the whole replicated\n[T, 10240] stream tensor before slicing, an extra full-size allocation and\ncopy per rank that the returned view kept alive. Slice this rank's rows\nfirst and pad only that slice; unpadded shards stay views.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: madhang <leiwu103@amd.com>",
