          "id": "b117d4c2d6dc03977c315f8bc7772c0c32b68ecf",
          "message": "perf(qwen3.5): Triton top-k router + pad the 513-row MoE router weight to 528 (#2707)\n\n* perf(qwen3.5): renormalize=False for Triton top-k router + pad 513-row MoE gate to 528\n\nExtends the Triton softmax top-k router (#2665) with two Qwen3.5 features:\n\n1. renormalize=False: the softmax denominator covers all N experts, not just\n   the K winners. Adds a RENORMALIZE constexpr to the kernel and passes it\n   through topK → triton_topk_softmax. The auto-gate now accepts both\n   renormalize values.\n\n2. output_row_alignment on MergedReplicatedLinear: the 512-expert +\n   1 shared-gate row (N=513) has no tuned GEMM and FlyDSL hgemm rejects\n   odd N. Padded to 528 rows after loading; forward returns the unpadded\n   width. Row views and supports_out() respect the padding.\n\nAlso replaces libdevice.exp with tl.exp for Triton interpreter compatibility\nin CI (triton 3.8.0 from PyPI has no HIP backend).\n\n* fix(test): tolerate interpreter tl.max tie-breaking on -inf experts\n\nThe Triton interpreter's tl.max on int64 keys may break ties among -inf\nexperts in a different order than torch.sort(stable=True). The picked set\nis the same and all get weight 0, so relax the id ordering check for the\nneg_inf test case while still verifying the set and the weights.\n\n* fix(router): exclude NaN logits from renormalize=False denominator\n\nWhen renormalize=False the full softmax denominator sums exp(x_i) over\nall experts. A NaN logit produces exp(NaN)=NaN which poisons the sum.\nThe reference treats NaN as -inf (weight 0); do the same by masking\nNaN positions out of the sum with tl.where.\n\n* revert: remove Triton router CI step from pre-checks.yaml\n\nThe CI workflow change should not be part of this PR.\n\n* remove test_topk_softmax_triton.py\n\nThis test file required a CI workflow change to run the interpreter\ntests and GPU+aiter for the rest. Not appropriate for this PR.\n\n* refactor: restore top-level imports per reviewer feedback\n\nMove triton_topk_softmax import back to module level in topK.py and\nrestore libdevice.exp usage in triton_topk_softmax.py, matching the\nexisting codebase convention. Tests that need CPU CI use\npytest.importorskip, not lazy imports in production code.\n\n* remove unnecessary output_row_alignment unit test\n\nThe padding logic is already validated end-to-end through model accuracy\ntests. A CPU-only unit test for this adds maintenance burden without\ncatching real regressions.\n\n* style: fix import sorting for ruff",
