          "id": "9fec99786b088168aec7729858c1176e99d818e6",
          "message": "perf(dsv41): add the shared expert output in the MegaMoE combine on the mori v2 EP path (#3132)\n\n* perf(dsv41): add the shared expert output in the MegaMoE combine on the mori v2 EP path\n\nOn the MegaMoE (mori v2 modular kernel) EP path the shared expert output\nwas joined after the routed combine and added with a separate elementwise\nadd. It is now handed to MegaMoE as a PendingSharedAdd; the combine waits\non its event right before the reduce and adds it there. The router GEMM is\nissued before the shared expert so the routed chain keeps the launch\nstream under graph replay. When the installed aiter MegaMoE does not take\nshared_add/shared_ready, or the comm-fused backend takes the step, the\noutput is added as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(moe): FusedMoE owns the shared-output handoff to the combine; test it\n\n- FusedMoE.combine_accepts_shared(rows) answers whether the routed combine\n  can add a shared-expert output on a step (MegaMoE behind the mori v2\n  modular kernel, off the comm-fused path); FusedMoE.with_shared_add(pending)\n  hands it over for one forward and always clears it, and\n  pending_shared_add() is what the quant method reads. PendingSharedAdd\n  moves next to FusedMoE. The DeepSeek-V4 MoE no longer reaches into the\n  experts' private state.\n- CPU tests: the shared output is added exactly once whether the combine\n  consumes it or leaves it to the caller, the handoff is cleared afterwards,\n  and combine_accepts_shared refuses without the mori v2 kernel and on\n  comm-fused steps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(moe): pass the shared output to the MegaMoE combine explicitly\n\nAddress review on the shared-in-combine path:\n\n- Drop the inspect.signature probe of MegaMoE.forward and the\n  PendingSharedAdd.consumed fallback. aiter main's MegaMoEGfx1250.forward\n  takes shared_add / shared_ready (ROCm/aiter#7661), so\n  MoriV2ModularKernel always passes them to MegaMoE; its Triton-experts\n  branch, which drives MegaMoE's internals instead of its forward, adds\n  the shared output after its combine.\n- Drop the with_shared_add / pending_shared_add attribute side channel.\n  FusedMoE.forward_maybe_comm_fused now hands shared_partial down its\n  non-comm-fused branch when the caller passes shared_ready:\n  forward_impl -> _run_experts -> Mxfp4MoEMethod.apply -> the modular\n  kernel, as explicit arguments. That call goes to forward_impl directly,\n  as the comm-fused backend does, because the moe_forward custom op cannot\n  carry the event; the caller is already inside its opaque dual-stream op.\n  combine_accepts_shared also refuses the steps where a later reduction\n  would count the shared output again (SP MegaMoE, PCP merge, simulated\n  DP, reduce_results), and an expert path without such a combine raises\n  instead of dropping the shared output.\n- Drop _dual_stream_shared_in_combine. dual_stream_moe_forward branches\n  on combine_accepts_shared and keeps routing through\n  routed_expert_forward(x, shared_partial=shared, shared_ready=...), so\n  the V4.1 override (fixed-order router) still applies; that override\n  forwards shared_ready.\n\nTests: the dual-stream handoff, forward_maybe_comm_fused with and without\nshared_ready, the combine_accepts_shared refusals, and both\nMoriV2ModularKernel branches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(moe): drive the shared-output handoff through the real forward_impl\n\nThe handoff test mocked forward_impl, so a hop that stopped passing\nshared_add/shared_ready on the way to the quant method would go unnoticed.\nRun the real forward_maybe_comm_fused -> forward_impl (-> forward_impl_graph\non several DP ranks) -> _run_experts chain against a recording quant method,\ncheck the ordinary forward hands it no shared output, and cover the\nMxfp4MoEMethod.apply guard for paths without a combine that adds it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [MoE] Describe both shared-add branches; wait on the event unconditionally\n\nThe MoriV2ModularKernel.forward docstring now says where the shared\noutput is added on each branch: inside MegaMoE's combine on its own\nforward, and after the combine on the triton_mega_moe branch, which\ndrives MegaMoE's internals. On that branch shared_ready always comes\nwith shared_add (forward_maybe_comm_fused sends neither or both), so the\nwait no longer checks for None and a future caller cannot get an\nunsynchronized add.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(moe): Mxfp4MoEMethod.apply hands the shared output to fused_experts\n\nThe last hop of the shared-output handoff: on the modular-kernel path\napply passes shared_add and shared_ready on to fused_experts, and passes\nneither when there is no shared output. A recording fused_experts checks\nboth cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
