          "id": "7a79a1476e4096a5c86f3ae9cba08f12e2fc91cb",
          "message": "fix(api): keep history tool-call arguments as strings for templates that concatenate them (#3345)\n\n* fix(api): keep history tool-call arguments as strings for templates that concatenate them\n\nDeepSeek-R1/V3's chat template concatenates tool['function']['arguments'].\nATOM parses history arguments into a mapping for every template but\nKimi-K3's, so each turn after a tool call failed with TypeError (HTTP 500).\nProbe the template at startup and keep the strings when it refuses the\nmapping but renders the string.\n\n* test(api): cover the tool-call argument probe at startup; note why custom encoders skip it\n\n* test(api): restore every setup global in the probe test; say R1/V3 take argument strings too\n\nParametrize the existing setup test over the two template checks instead of a\nsecond copy that leaked api_server globals into later tests. Update the\ncomments that said only Kimi-K3 keeps argument strings, write the flag as\nkeeps or needs_strings, and test a ChatMessage history through\napply_chat_template plus a template that refuses both forms.",
