          "distinct": true,
          "id": "273c78de59137688027acf74633c56b0c9c9ee62",
          "message": "fix(ci): resolve labelled benchmark variants in the regression rerun matrix (#3079)\n\n* fix(ci): resolve labelled benchmark variants in the regression rerun matrix\n\nregression_rerun.py derived the variant only from a trailing \"-mtp<N>\" on\nthe report's model name and compared model_id with the catalog path\nverbatim. The nightly report carries the catalog display name of the\nvariant (e.g. \"DeepSeek-V4-Pro DPA DSpark\") and the served checkpoint\nunder the /models/ mount (e.g.\n\"/models/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-DSpark\"), so labelled variants\n(MTP3, DPA, DPA MTP3, DPA TBO, DPA DSpark, DSpark, EAGLE3, MegaMoE) were\nnot found. The top-N cut ran before matching, so the most severe,\nunmatched entries could leave the rerun matrix empty, and the\n[Perf Regression] issue was then never filed.\n\n- Match the report's model name against the catalog's own variant\n  expansion (load_variants display), restricted to records whose path\n  equals model_id with the /models/ mount stripped (this honours\n  variant-level path overrides); pick between variants that share a\n  display by concurrency band; return None unless exactly one record\n  matches. Names without benchmark_model_name\n  (\"<checkpoint basename>[-mtp<N>]\") still match basename + suffix.\n- Resolve every regression first, then take the N most severe resolved\n  ones, so an unmappable entry does not use up a rerun slot.\n- Name rerun configs/cells prefix + suffix so two variants of one model\n  do not share trace dirs and artifact names, and keep cell names unique\n  (a repeated name gets the first \"-<n>\" no other cell uses).\n- Run profiler-analysis, which files the [Perf Regression] issue,\n  whenever a regression was detected, even if no rerun cell was\n  generated, and drop the unused noqa on the catalog import.\n- Add CPU tests using catalog identities and workload shapes from a\n  nightly report, with synthetic severity data, in\n  benchmark-artifacts-tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Yaakoub El Khamra <176948988+yelkhamra@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ci): report ambiguous regression-rerun matches; clarify synthetic fixtures\n\nThe resolver returned no record both when nothing matched a report entry\nand when several variants survived the concurrency-band filter (variants\nsharing a display with overlapping conc_min/conc_max bands, or an entry\nwithout a concurrency). generate_configs printed \"No model config found\"\nfor both, which hid a catalog error behind an unknown-model warning.\n\nReturn every matching record and let generate_configs report the two\ncases apart: the no-match message is unchanged, and several records now\nprint \"ambiguous model config ...: N candidates\" with each candidate's\ncheckpoint, suffix and concurrency band, so the catalog entry can be\nfound. The entry is still skipped and still does not use up a rerun\nslot; the job does not fail hard.\n\nThe test fixture comment now says its shapes are modelled on the catalog\nand partly synthetic instead of \"copied from\" models.json: the current\ncatalog has no DPA MTP3 V4-Pro variant, and the DSpark / EPLB / MiniMax\nconfig, extra_args and env_vars are trimmed. The report test comment no\nlonger claims a real nightly run, since the severities are synthetic. A\nnew test covers an overlapping-band ambiguity and a no-match entry.\n\nSigned-off-by: Yaakoub El Khamra <176948988+yelkhamra@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ci): report incomplete regression entries before matching; fix docstring\n\ngenerate_configs checked isl/osl/conc completeness after resolving the\nentry. For an entry with no concurrency whose display is shared by two\ncatalog variants, resolution returned both candidates, so the entry was\nreported as \"ambiguous model config ... at conc ?\" even though the catalog\nwas valid and only the report entry was incomplete. Check completeness\nfirst: such an entry now prints \"missing isl/osl/conc\" and is still\nskipped without using up a rerun slot. With conc guaranteed present past\nthat check, the ambiguous message prints it directly and the \"?\" fallback\nis gone.\n\nThe catalog-error comment no longer claims an entry without a concurrency\nis a catalog error. The _find_model_configs docstring says the caller\nreports zero and several differently, and states that an entry without a\nconcurrency returns every candidate and is reported as incomplete before\nresolution.\n\nNew test: an entry without conc for the shared-display EPLB pair prints\nthe incomplete warning and not \"ambiguous\", and does not consume the one\nrerun slot.\n\nSigned-off-by: Yaakoub El Khamra <176948988+yelkhamra@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Yaakoub El Khamra <176948988+yelkhamra@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Yaakoub El Khamra <176948988+yelkhamra@users.noreply.github.com>",
