          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1207c1eedc5f545e40a5852182dbb1242f5c1fc4",
          "message": "ci(sglang): trim SGLang cases, run each MI355 case once a week, stop nightlies still running at 09:00 Beijing time (#3305)\n\n* ci(sglang): drop V4-Pro MTP1, GLM-5.2 PCP4, the OOB_P2 tier and V3.2 cases other than FP8 TP4\n\nRemoved from the SGLang benchmark and accuracy workflows and from their\ncatalogs (sglang_benchmark_models.json, sglang_models_accuracy.json):\n\n- DeepSeek-V4-Pro MTP1 TP8\n- GLM-5.2 FP8 TP4 PCP4\n- every OOB_P2 model on MI355: DeepSeek-R1 (all variants, including the\n  accuracy-only FP8 TP4 Online Quant), Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-FP8 TP4/TP8,\n  Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B-Quark-MXFP4 TP8, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8 TP2 and\n  GLM-5.1 FP8 TP8\n- DeepSeek-V3.2 FP8 TP4 DP4 EP4, TP8 and TP8 DP8 EP8 (FP8 TP4 stays)\n\nThe OOB_P2 tier and its manual option are gone; the Saturday schedule now\nruns P0 + P1 like Tue/Thu. Benchmark-catalog templates used only by the\nremoved models are dropped, and so is the test that only checked the\nremoved R1 / V3.2 DP-EP configs. MI308 cases are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(sglang): stop scheduled SGLang runs still going at 09:00 Beijing time\n\nA new workflow fires daily at 01:00 UTC. It cancels any scheduled\natom-sglang-benchmark / atom-sglang-accuracy-validation run that has not\ncompleted, waits up to 5 minutes, then force-cancels whatever is left. The\nplain cancel comes first so the GPU jobs' `if: always()` container cleanup\nstill runs; force-cancel skips it. Manually dispatched runs are not touched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(sglang): drop DeepSeek-V3.2 FP8 TP4 from the SGLang benchmark and accuracy runs\n\nThe last DeepSeek-V3.2 case goes from both workflows and their catalogs;\nOOB_P1 is now MiniMax-M3-MXFP8 EAGLE3 TP4 MTP3 alone. The aiter_runtime and\ndeepseek_common benchmark-catalog templates were only used by it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(sglang): run each MI355 benchmark / accuracy case once a week, spread over the nights\n\nBoth workflows now have one cron per weekday, and a MI355_WEEKLY_SCHEDULE\nkeyed by it names the MI355 cases that night runs:\n\n- benchmark (23:00 Beijing): one OOB_P0 / OOB_P1 model a night, Mon-Sun;\n  MI308 still runs Mon-Sat.\n- accuracy (00:00 Beijing, filed under the evening before): one or two\n  MI355 models a night; MI308 still runs every night.\n\nA night's benchmark and accuracy cover different models. Manual runs are\nunchanged. tests/test_sglang_weekly_schedule.py runs each workflow's own\nselection for every cron and checks each MI355 case lands once a week and\nMI308 keeps its cadence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(sglang): give MI308 its own scheduled runs and exempt them from the 09:00 deadline\n\nGitHub cancels whole runs, not jobs, so MI308 now runs apart from MI355:\nbenchmark MI308 on '0 15 * * 1-6', accuracy MI308 on '0 16 * * *', and the\nper-weekday crons select MI355 only. run-name titles scheduled runs\n\"(scheduled MI308)\" / \"(scheduled MI355)\", and the deadline workflow only\ncancels \"(scheduled MI355)\" runs. The concurrency group now includes the\ncron, so a night's MI355 and MI308 runs do not queue behind each other.\n\nThe accuracy MI355 dropdown gains the DeepSeek-V4-Pro TP8 and MTP3 TP8\ncases it was missing, and the test checks both dropdowns list every case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(sglang): make the nightly deadline job fail when it cannot list or stop runs\n\nReview on #3305 found the deadline job stayed green while runs kept going:\na failed list of one workflow silently skipped it (or exited before\ncancelling the other), and failed cancel / force-cancel calls were\nswallowed by `|| true`.\n\nNow each workflow is listed on its own: a failed list fails the job, but\nthe other workflow's runs are still cancelled. A failed plain cancel only\nwarns, since the force-cancel after the grace period covers the run; a\nrefused force-cancel fails the job, and so does any run still unfinished\nSETTLE_SECONDS after the force-cancel.\n\ntests/test_sglang_nightly_deadline.py runs the step's Bash against a fake\n`gh`; five of its eight cases fail on the previous script.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
