          "distinct": true,
          "id": "19c292fe2a1ee333d29f4a630bda9508e74d7da8",
          "message": "ci(vllm): run each vLLM nightly benchmark / accuracy case once a week; stop scheduled vLLM runs at 09:00 Beijing time (#3459)\n\n* ci(vllm): run each vLLM benchmark / accuracy case once a week\n\nBenchmark: the Mon/Wed/Fri 23:30 Beijing nightly ran the same six models\nevery time. It now has one cron per night, and WEEKLY_SCHEDULE gives each\nnight two of them, so each model runs once a week. Manual runs, including\nthe ALL group, are unchanged.\n\nAccuracy: the 00:00 Beijing nightly ran all 41 nightly cases every night.\nEach nightly entry of oot_models_accuracy.json now names the Beijing\nweekday it runs on (nightly_weekday, added to the catalog schema), and the\nscheduled run keeps only that day's cases: 5-7 a night, one model family\nper night. The priority slots, weekend ordering and validation window are\nunchanged. A nightly entry without a weekday fails the run.\n\ntests/test_vllm_weekly_schedule.py runs both workflows' own selection for\nevery night and checks each case lands once a week; all three cases fail\non the previous workflows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(vllm): run the vLLM benchmark nightly Mon-Sat and stop it at 09:00 Beijing time\n\nThe vLLM benchmark now runs every night but Sunday at 23:30 Beijing, one\nof its six scheduled models a night, so each still runs once a week.\nIts scheduled runs are titled \"(scheduled MI355)\", and the nightly\ndeadline lists atom-vllm-benchmark.yaml next to the SGLang workflows, so\na vLLM benchmark still running at 09:00 Beijing time is stopped the same\nway. The vLLM accuracy nightly is left out: its jobs already gate on the\nBeijing day they belong to.\n\nThe deadline now covers more than SGLang, so it is renamed\natom-sglang-nightly-deadline.yaml -> atom-nightly-deadline.yaml (and its\ntest to tests/test_nightly_deadline.py), and its fake `gh` covers every\nworkflow in WORKFLOWS.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(vllm): stop the vLLM accuracy nightly at 09:00 Beijing time; drop its 150-min skip\n\nThe vLLM accuracy nightly's scheduled runs are now titled\n\"(scheduled MI355)\" and the nightly deadline lists the workflow, so a run\nstill going at 09:00 Beijing time is cancelled like the SGLang ones and\nthe vLLM benchmark.\n\nEach accuracy job used to skip itself when fewer than 150 minutes of the\nBeijing day were left. With the run stopped at 09:00 that cannot\nhappen, so the check is removed; the job still skips when the Beijing\ndate no longer matches the scheduled run's.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(vllm): check nightly_weekday at PR time; test each accuracy night against it\n\nReview on #3459:\n- validate_catalog.py now fails a nightly oot_models_accuracy.json entry\n  without nightly_weekday, so the omission is caught at PR time rather\n  than by the workflow refusing the whole night.\n- The accuracy schedule test checks each night's cases against their\n  nightly_weekday, not only that every case lands once a week; a mapping\n  shifted by a day now fails it.\n- A scheduled vLLM benchmark's selected_group is \"<night> weekly\": the\n  variable also names a manual run's group (ALL), so it keeps its name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
