          "distinct": true,
          "id": "9cc9498b19dd123a956e27e0a693df14ba2c4f3e",
          "message": "ci(atomesh): drop MI350X nightly, free busy GPUs on idle nodes, unprivileged RDMA smoke (#3208)\n\n* ci: remove Atomesh Spur MI350X nightly schedule\n\n* ci: remove stopped containers on Atomesh nodes before manual runs\n\n* ci: run Atomesh containers without --privileged\n\nThe Slurm-path server container and the Mooncake RDMA smoke container now\nget only the devices and capabilities they use, like the Spur path. The\nserver container adds SYS_NICE so Docker's default seccomp still allows\nset_mempolicy and mbind for NUMA placement.\n\n* test(atomesh): expect MoRI IO accuracy as the only schedule\n\nThe Spur MI350X nightly cron is gone, so the schedule tests now check that\nthe MoRI IO cron is the only one, runs on the Spur lane, and keeps its own\nconcurrency group.\n\n* ci: kill GPU holders on idle nodes instead of removing stopped containers\n\nRemoving every stopped container also deleted other users' containers on\nshared Spur nodes. Manual runs now act only when a node's GPUs are busy and\nthe scheduler shows no other job on it: every process with the GPUs open is\nkilled, through docker kill when it runs in a container. On the Slurm path,\nwhere the allocation is exclusive, this joins the existing per-node srun.\n\n* ci: keep --privileged on the Slurm-path Atomesh server container\n\nNo run has exercised the non-Spur srun launch without it (NUMA binding and\nRDMA), so restore it there. The Mooncake RDMA smoke container stays\nunprivileged; run 42994195521 passed with it.\n\n* test(atomesh): drop EVENT_SCHEDULE and the MI350X nightly subtest\n\nThe workflow no longer reads EVENT_SCHEDULE, and the 10 16 cron is gone, so\nthe V4 test only checks that push runs exclude the weekly V4 cases, and the\nconcurrency group test is named for the only schedule left.\n\n* ci: kill GPU holders on Spur nodes whatever VRAM they hold\n\nThe Spur path used to act only once a GPU went over ATOMESH_GPU_BUSY_MB.\nNow any process with the GPUs open on a node that runs no other job is\nkilled before the idle wait, as on the Slurm path.\n\n* ci: cancel other users' jobs that share a node's GPUs before a manual run\n\nBefore, a manual run left a node's GPU holders alone when squeue listed\nanother job on it or did not answer. Now it scancels other users' running\njobs on the node and then kills the GPU holders; when squeue does not\nanswer, it kills the holders anyway. A job of the same CI user on the node,\nsuch as a sibling cell, still leaves everything alone. kill_gpu_holders no\nlonger aborts a set -e caller when a lookup comes back empty.\n\n* ci: kill GPU holders on allocated nodes instead of cancelling jobs\n\nThe node was handed to this job, so whatever still holds its GPUs is\nkilled, whether or not squeue lists another job there or answers at all.\nOther users' Slurm jobs are no longer scancelled. A job of the same CI user\non the node, such as a sibling cell, still leaves the GPUs alone.\n\n* ci(atomesh): log when no process holds the GPUs before a run\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ci(atomesh): test the GPU-holder kill and reuse slurm_cmd\n\nThe preflight tests start a real process behind a fake KFD list and\nsqueue, and check that a manual run kills it beside another user's job,\nwhen squeue fails, and with only its own job listed, keeps it beside a\nsibling job of the same user, and that other runs leave it alone.\nATOMESH_KFD_PROC_DIR lets the tests point at that list. A workflow test\nchecks ATOMESH_KILL_GPU_HOLDERS is 1 only for workflow_dispatch.\n\nThe comments now say what the kill does on Spur, which may co-schedule\nother users' jobs. spur_controller_job_state calls slurm_cmd, and the\nMoRI IO schedule helpers drop their one-valued schedule parameter.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ci(atomesh): log other jobs only when their GPU holders are killed\n\nfree_gpus_for_this_job said another user's GPU processes were killed even\nwhen a later sibling job of the same user kept them. The Kimi K3 profile\ncomment no longer says the schedule runs nightly.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
