          "id": "16d10f44d692bff5bc50745e8d6580d1b960a2a7",
          "message": "fix(ci): cache the draft model under /models instead of downloading it at every launch (#3517)\n\nA speculative-decoding accuracy case passes its draft as a Hub id\n(--draft-model Inferact/Kimi-K3.1-DSpark), so the server downloads the\n~5 GiB checkpoint on every launch into the throwaway container's HF\ncache. That download goes through hf-xet, which intermittently stalls:\nmost runs take ~5s, but 118s, 250s and 836s were observed, all spent\nsilently in \"Waiting for ATOM server to be ready\".\n\nThe Download models step now also caches the draft under /models/<id>\nwith the existing lock-protected script (Xet off for this one fetch),\nand the launch points --draft-model at that directory. If caching\nfails the launch falls back to the Hub id as before.",
