          "id": "ceee3ba95149decd4a9143051bec838839b70b74",
          "message": "ci: start heavy PR CI only when the gate opens, and keep unrelated label events from cancelling it (#3490)\n\n* ci: start heavy PR CI only when the gate opens, and keep unrelated label events from cancelling it\n\n* test: black formatting in test_heavy_ci_gate.py\n\n* test(atomesh): let the workflow expression helper read ! and labels.*.name\n\n* ci(gate): fail the gate on a rerun of a superseded gate-opening label run\n\n* ci(gate): decide label reruns by their payload and keep no-op runs from hiding a replaced PR run\n\n- A rerun replays the event payload, which also fixes the run's\n  concurrency group and gate check name, so a rerun of a labeled event is\n  decided by that payload: a no-op label run stays a no-op whatever the\n  live labels say (it could otherwise start heavy CI outside the PR\n  group), and a gate-opening run is re-judged like a code-change rerun on\n  the PR's live state. Replaces the undecidable superseded-run rule.\n- detect_replaced_pr_run skips no-op label runs when it looks for the PR\n  group's latest pull_request run. atom-test names a no-op run's first job\n  \"Check Heavy CI Gate (no-op label)\" (CI_GATE_NOOP_JOB), which exists\n  from the run's start, unlike the gate check, which is created last.\n- The label lookup fails closed (labels-query-failed) when the payload has\n  no labels and the live query fails.\n- CI_GATE_LABELS is parsed once into GATE_LABELS; find_allowed_pr_label\n  takes the labels to search; comments and header describe the rule.\n- Tests evaluate workflow expressions with atomesh_workflow_helpers'\n  github_expressions (now also label events and needs outputs) instead of\n  a second evaluator.\n\n* ci: count the added label as on the PR, and look past queued no-op runs\n\nA labeled payload whose label list lacks the label it added made the\nscript and the workflows' group/gate-name expressions disagree. A no-op\nlabel run still queued (no jobs yet) hid the PR run an approval replaced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
