          "distinct": true,
          "id": "17edc61575fd87b2aac9a7dfd94b532c07fc52fe",
          "message": "[MiniMax-M3.1] LMCache offload with an NVFP4 KV and a DSpark draft of its own dtype (#3591)\n\n* [MiniMax-M3.1] LMCache offload with an NVFP4 KV and an fp8 DSpark draft\n\nThree startup / metadata gates kept --kv-cache-dtype nvfp4 + DSpark from running\nunder the in-process lmcache_offload connector (ATOM_KV_OFFLOAD=lmcache):\n\n- config: a MiniMax-M3 own-pool draft may keep a KV dtype different from the\n  target under lmcache_offload. M3 PAGE bytes are published pool -> field ->\n  layer with the draft pages after the target, and the PAGE namespace hashes\n  the whole speculative_config, draft KV dtype included, so a store written\n  with another draft dtype is never read back. Other offload layouts and P/D\n  connectors still refuse.\n- minimax_m3/config: NVFP4 KV is allowed under lmcache_offload. An NVFP4 page\n  holds its data and e4m3 scales inline (the per-layer global K/V scale is a\n  constant 1.0) and the NVFP4 index entry is one page, so both move as opaque\n  per-block bytes. MXFP4 and P/D connectors (which reshard by head runs) still\n  refuse.\n- offload/config: FP4 KV dtypes map to uint8 in the LMCache base metadata\n  (aiter has no nvfp4 torch dtype; the raw-byte wrapper reports uint8 anyway).\n\nTests: an MXFP4 target beside offload is refused by its own KV rule whatever\nits draft; NVFP4 under lmcache_offload starts with an fp8 or a default (bf16)\nDSpark draft; NVFP4 under a P/D connector is still refused, and so is a draft\ndtype beside it; the resolver gives an NVFP4 target's own-pool draft bf16 by\ndefault and the requested fp8.\n\n* [MiniMax-M3.1] NVFP4 offload: one leaf-wise connector predicate for both gates\n\nReview of the previous commit (ROCm/ATOM#3235):\n\n- minimax_m3/config: `NVFP4_PAGE_CONNECTORS` and `_connectors_move_nvfp4_pages`\n  read the transports through `KVConnectorFactory.leaf_connectors`, so an alias\n  (`LMCacheConnectorV1`) and a `multi` of them pass, and a `multi` with any leaf\n  outside the set is refused.\n  `nvfp4_pages_move` is the one rule both the NVFP4 KV refusal and the\n  draft-dtype gate in `Config` read.\n- The draft-dtype gate lets an own-pool MiniMax-M3 draft of another dtype run\n  only beside an NVFP4 KV whose transports pass that rule; an MXFP4 target still\n  meets the gate (its test is back to #3235's), and its error text names the\n  exception.\n- The refusal comment states the real reason: those paths are not verified.\n- offload/config: `FP4_CACHE_DTYPES` instead of a literal pair.\n- docs/configuration_guide.md (`kv_cache_dtype`, the draft-dtype paragraph) and\n  the `validate_runtime_config` docstring state the exception.\n- tests: the NVFP4 cache tests import `no_synthetic_acceptance_import`, which\n  keeps triton out of `SpeculativeConfig` (Pre Checkin has none); new cases for\n  the alias, `multi[lmcache_offload]`, `multi[moriio, lmcache_offload]` and\n  MXFP4 under lmcache_offload.\n\n* [MiniMax-M3.1] NVFP4 offload: a draft dtype only for a DSpark draft under lmcache_offload\n\nReview of the previous two commits (ROCm/ATOM#3591):\n\n- minimax_m3/config: `draft_dtype_moves` is the draft-dtype gate's own rule: an\n  NVFP4 KV, a DSpark draft, and every transport (`multi` expanded) in\n  `DRAFT_DTYPE_CONNECTORS` (`lmcache_offload`). An M3 EAGLE3 draft of another\n  dtype is refused again, and a transport added to `NVFP4_PAGE_CONNECTORS`\n  does not join it. `nvfp4_pages_move` speaks for the target's pages only.\n- config: the comment says what holds: a store written with another draft dtype\n  is never read back (draft and target pages share one key per chunk). The\n  refusal names the M3 exception only to an M3 target.\n- docs/configuration_guide.md: an own-pool draft beside an FP4 KV is bf16, or\n  fp8 with `--spec-decode-kv-cache-dtype fp8`; the draft-dtype exception is\n  DSpark under the in-process LMCache offload only.\n- tests: an EAGLE3 draft beside NVFP4 under lmcache_offload is refused; a\n  connector that moves NVFP4 pages (Mooncake, patched into the set) still\n  refuses a draft dtype; a Llama target's refusal does not name the M3\n  exception; `build_lmcache_metadata` reports fp4 / nvfp4 pages as uint8.\n\n* [MiniMax-M3.1] One helper for a KV cache's torch dtype\n\nReview of #3591 (ganyi1996ppo, offload/config.py:789): the FP4-to-uint8 choice\nis a function, and every place that maps a KV / index cache dtype string to a\ntorch dtype calls it.\n\n- atom/config.py: `kv_cache_torch_dtype(kv_cache_dtype)` returns uint8 for\n  `FP4_CACHE_DTYPES` (packed bytes, which aiter's `d_dtypes` has no entry\n  for), else aiter's entry. aiter is imported only for the second case.\n- Callers: the LMCache base metadata (offload/config.py), the MHA pool and\n  the index cache spec (aiter_attention.py; the pool picked uint8 by \"has an\n  FP4 layout\", which is set exactly for an FP4 KV), the MLA builder and pool\n  (aiter_mla.py), the draft's own pool (spec_decode/draft_kv.py), and the\n  vLLM plugin's KV dtype lookups. Unchanged for every dtype these reach today;\n  the sglang / rtp-llm lookups of a literal \"fp8\" / \"bf16\" stay as they are.\n- tests/test_kv_cache_dtype_config.py: fp4 / nvfp4 give uint8; bf16 / fp8\n  give aiter's entry (a stub aiter, so the CPU lane needs none).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ganyi <ygan@amd.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
