          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ecec81921da0c27a088d542fcefad51fe83e4d5a",
          "message": "fix(moriio): keep answering the remote-prefill lookup until the receive is queued (#3570)\n\n* fix(moriio): keep answering the remote-prefill lookup until the receive is queued\n\n`get_num_new_matched_tokens` answered \"load the whole prompt remotely\"\nonly once per request (`kv_async_tagged`). The scheduler asks on every\npass that considers a request and can hold it back after a yes, for\nexample when the decode's running set is full. The next pass then got\n\"nothing to load\", and the request ran a local prefill on the decode\nside instead of receiving its KV:\n\n- The producer kept the request's blocks and state slot, waiting for a\n  WRITE_REQ that never came, so a saturated decode filled the producer's\n  state pool and stalled it.\n- With a draft model the decode crashed: the remote-prefill allocation\n  skips the draft lookahead blocks, and `_check_draft_writes_allocated`\n  refused the local prefill (\"27 blocks ... do not reach position ...\").\n\nAnswer yes as long as `do_remote_prefill` is set; `update_state_after_alloc`\nclears it once the receive is queued. Same fix as in the unmerged\nROCm/ATOM#3478.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address review: CPU-lane lookup guard, Mooncake latch, offload stub\n\n- tests/test_moriio_connector.py: the regression runs on the CPU lane\n  (`RemotePrefillLookupTest` lifts `get_num_new_matched_tokens` and\n  `update_state_after_alloc` from the source): ask, ask, alloc, ask. It\n  passes here and fails on main. The aiter-gated copy is dropped.\n- Mooncake's lookup drops the `kv_async_tagged` check: MoRIIO was its only\n  writer, so the two twin lookups now read the same.\n- test_a_multi_connector_cancel_re_arms_honestly: the MoRIIO stub stops\n  matching only after a simulated `update_state_after_alloc`, as the\n  docstring says.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address review: one AST lifting helper, honest composite docstring\n\n`load_function` takes a keyword-only `cls` to lift a method instead of\na second helper copying it. The multi cancel test's docstring no longer\ncalls `[moriio, lmcache_offload]` a supported setup: `validate_multi_config`\nrefuses a P/D consumer beside an offload tier, so the test pins the\ncomposite's cancel contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(moriio): give the lookup test's fake consumer its mode and paging\n\n`RemotePrefillLookupTest` runs the real `update_state_after_alloc` on a\nfake consumer. A kept-prefix receive reads the consumer's transfer mode,\nblock size, DCP size and page geometry, and the request's cached tokens,\nso the fakes carry them and the test holds whichever change lands first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
