          "distinct": true,
          "id": "cbf1617468110a81e720a00021c5d3c5e14ce232",
          "message": "ci(atomesh): Mooncake Store decode owners on every decode-only node, packed_nodes included (#3514)\n\n* feat(ci): let packed_nodes cells put Mooncake Store owners on the decode node\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* feat(ci): put Mooncake Store decode owners on every decode-only node\n\nMOONCAKE_STORE_DECODE_OWNERS was limited to one decode node, because the\npools counted the decode owners once. Count them once per node that starts\nthem instead: every decode node under multi_node (yD x\nDECODE_NODES_PER_WORKER), and each node with decode workers only under\npacked_nodes, where the previous commit has that node's first decode worker\nstart them. The prefill node and every decode node then wait for the same\ntotal. One prefill worker is still required, since all owners join its\nnode's masters, and the other layouts stay refused.\n\nThe packed guard reads ATOMESH_PD_WORKER_LAYOUT, as the capacity count does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(atomesh): let a decode node's Store wait allow for the other decode nodes' compaction\n\nWith several decode-owner nodes, the total each decode node waits for\nincludes the owners of the other decode nodes, which mount only once those\nnodes have compacted their memory. That wait still used\nMOONCAKE_STORE_WAIT_TIMEOUT alone, so a node that compacted sooner could\ngive up and stop its owners while a peer was still compacting within its\nbudget. It now waits mooncake_store_cross_node_timeout\nMOONCAKE_STORE_DECODE_OWNERS, as the prefill node's wait for the same total\nalready does. A test staggers a second decode node's owners past the plain\nwait.\n\nmooncake_decode_owner_nodes returned a number; it is now\nmooncake_decode_owner_node_count. The rule that a packed prefill's node\nstarts no decode owners was written in both the count and the start; both\nnow ask mooncake_node_starts_decode_owners, and a node starts its owners\nonce whatever the layout. prefill_single_node stays refused, now under\ntest: with the one prefill worker the decode owners allow, it puts the\nworkers on the same nodes as multi_node.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(atomesh): refuse Store decode owners with a prefill worker on two nodes\n\nUnder pd_worker_layout multi_node every node of a prefill worker runs\nstart_prefill, so each starts a Store of its own: masters on its own host,\nthen a wait for MOONCAKE_STORE_OWNERS plus every decode node's\nMOONCAKE_STORE_DECODE_OWNERS. The decode owners join NODE0_ADDR only, so\nwith PREFILL_NODES_PER_WORKER=2 the second prefill node's wait always timed\nout. check_mooncake_store_settings now refuses MOONCAKE_STORE_DECODE_OWNERS\nunless the one prefill worker sits on one node, and names prefill\nnodes_per_worker in the message. No catalog cell changes: the mcstore-2n\ncells run their prefill worker on one node.\n\nThe comments that still spoke of one decode node now speak of each decode\nnode, as do the refusal of Store settings in the decode role env and\nmooncake_store_cross_node_timeout's comment. The flag that starts a node's\ndecode owners once is declared with the other Store state and checked as\nsave_mooncake_store_metrics checks its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: wanzhenchn <wanzhenchn@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
