          "distinct": true,
          "id": "36adbfddb6379a038c2a6ac0ea2e3552607e507d",
          "message": "Reset the restore fields when a request gets a fresh allocation (#3323)\n\n## Problem\nAn earlier tier load leaves its restore state on a request: `offload_loaded`, `offload_load_failed`, `offload_loaded_tokens` and `offload_load_start_tokens`. A fresh allocation did not clear them, and a connector that plans no new load (a state-only tier load) never rewrites them. This affects every chunked-base tier connector, not only Store.\n\n1. **Restore, preempt, state-only re-park.** A request restored L tokens, was preempted, and its HBM prefix was evicted below L. It then re-parks on a state-only tier load at rung r < L. On wake, `_mark_offload_load_ready` sets `num_cached_tokens = L`. Rows r..L were never filled and are skipped, so the output is silently wrong. `pending_prefill_tokens` is also under-counted.\n2. **Failed load, re-park, abort.** The deallocate branch of `_consume_failed_remote_kv` leaves `offload_load_failed = True` with an empty block table. If the request then re-parks on a state-only load and is aborted, `terminal_consumed` is True and cleanup runs at once. The blocks are freed while the load is still writing into them, and the late report id leaks in `finished_recving_kv_req_ids`.\n3. **Restore, preempt, Store re-park, abort.** The original report. A stale `offload_loaded` made the abort free the blocks while a second Store load was still writing into them.\n\n## Fix\n`_allocate_admitted_prefill` resets all four fields right after `block_manager.allocate` succeeds. Phase 2 and early load both allocate through it. The reset runs before the connector is told of the allocation, which may set the token fields again. This covers every chunked-base tier load.\n\n## Tests\n- `test_a_state_only_repark_after_a_restore_is_not_woken_past_its_rung` (fails on main: `num_cached_tokens` is 44, not r).\n- `test_an_abort_after_a_failed_load_and_repark_waits_for_the_new_load` (fails on main: the abort cleans up at once).\n- `test_an_abort_after_preempt_waits_for_the_second_load` (fails on main).\n- Reverting any one of the resets makes a test fail.\n- Related scheduler, offload connector and state-checkpoint tests: no new failures against main. The 85 collection/setup errors are identical on main and come from a missing `msgpack`.\n\nOne commit on current `main`: 4 files, +187 / -3. The reset runs only when a KV connector is configured (only a connector's load sets these fields: planned by the connector, woken or failed by the scheduler), so the no-connector path is unchanged. Tests cover Phase 2 and the early-load admission.\n\nA request whose earlier load already settled and still holds its blocks resumes through `_is_offload_prefill_resume` and is not allocated again, so the reset never touches a load that just completed.",
