          "id": "3252233fec5cda721c46af039cef53182634df89",
          "message": "fix(pd): publish only the prompt's KV blocks from a Mooncake producer (#3589)\n\n* Mooncake producer: publish only the prompt's KV blocks\n\nWith deferred output a finished prefill is scheduled for one more step\nbefore its output finishes it, and that step's may_append adds a block\nwhenever the prompt fills its last block. request_finished published that\nblock too, so the consumer, which allocates the prompt's blocks only, got\none source block too many and the producer aborted the send on the block\ncount mismatch: the request failed on the decode side.\n\nPublish the prompt's blocks only, in both the save entry and\nremote_block_ids. The consumer computes the first token's KV itself.\n\n* Mooncake producer: name the published blocks prefill_block_ids\n\n* Mooncake producer: one helper for a request's prompt pages\n\nThe chunked save path and the published blocks both keep only the pages\nD allocates; compute them in one place.\n\n* Mooncake producer: state the send's page-count check exactly\n\nThe producer aborts the send unless D's destination page count equals\nceil(source pages / src_block_skip_factor), not only when P has more\npages. The prompt-block test also covers a prompt that ends one token\ninto a page.\n\n* Mooncake connector: describe the pending request entries\n\nEach entry is (Sequence, block ids, state slot). Recv and chunked save\nentries hold the full block table, which build_connector_meta trims for\na chunked save; a non-chunked save is queued already trimmed.",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-23T10:48:23+08:00",
