          "distinct": true,
          "id": "03244191644c2f6e977ae38871822d6b35ea5014",
          "message": "Add opt-in async Mooncake Store lease renewal (#3533)\n\nATOM_STORE_ASYNC_RENEW (default 0) renews the Store read leases of a\npending load on the bounded renewal executor of AsyncStoreLookup instead\nof waiting on the scheduler thread right before the load.\n_ensure_lookup_pin keeps the fresh-hit reuse and the token range, and\nends in _renew_before_load, which holds the synchronous renewal. With\nthe flag off, renew, _clear_pending_load and\nScheduler._finish_rejected_waiting are unchanged (renew_key_snapshot\nrepeats renew's three lines of range math so that renew stays as is). The async variants (_renew_before_load_async,\n_clear_pending_load_async, _build_connector_meta_async,\n_has_pending_work_async, _finish_rejected_waiting_cancelling) are bound\non the instance in __init__ only when the flag is on;\n_has_pending_work_async also counts loads handed to workers and not yet\nreported, since an idle or drain build can dispatch a parked GET. Two shared\nchanges run either way: the chunked build_connector_meta parks a PENDING\nload inside its existing `if not pinned:` branch (LookupPinStatus is\nfalsy), and AsyncStoreLookup's renewal executor is bounded\n(limit=capacity).\n\nAsyncStoreLookup.renew_async polls done() first; cancel_renewal cancels\nfirst. A load whose renewal has not finished goes out one or more steps\nlater; a fresh hit, a rejected submission or a new submission while an\nearlier renewal is still stuck dispatches in the same step, and a renewal\nalready queued behind a hung RPC stays parked until its own timeout. A\ntimeout, an exception, a cancelled or rejected renewal, or a renewal\nstill stuck from an earlier load falls back to dispatching the GET, as\nthe synchronous path does. A renewal miss is not a data-plane load\nfailure. Polls while parked and each fallback reason are counted\n(renew_parked, renew_fallback_<reason>). An abort before dispatch\ncancels the undispatched load.",
