          "id": "ecb2d3020a77721576abb13ec4b5768746ddd86a",
          "message": "fix(engine): yield the GIL in the engine loop so finished outputs ship at once (#3469)\n\n* fix(engine): yield the GIL in the engine loop so finished outputs ship at once\n\nEngineCore.busy_loop blocks nowhere on an idle pass, and nothing blocks between\nqueuing a step's outputs and the loop's next blocking call. While it spins it\nholds the GIL, so the output-sender thread -- woken to ship a finished\nrequest's last chunk -- runs only when CPython forces a switch, after\nsys.getswitchinterval() (5 ms by default). Every request's final streamed\nchunk sat that long in output_queue once the engine went idle, which adds\n~0.5 ms to the ITL of a 10-token turn; a new request's admission waited the\nsame way.\n\nAdd yield_gil() (time.sleep(0): drop and retake the GIL around a zero-length\nsleep) and call it on the idle passes of EngineCore.busy_loop and the PP head\nloop, and after a step's outputs are queued in EngineCore._postprocess and\nDecodeEngineCore._postprocess. The DP loop already blocks every pass in its\ncross-rank state sync, and the PP downstream stages block in recv_metadata.\n\nMeasured on 8x MI355X (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash TP8, DSpark 5, forced acceptance\n3.51, streaming chat): the final chunk's gap 7.5 -> 2.9 ms (one step), a\n10-token turn's ITL 1.42 -> 0.91 ms, AgentX c1 P90 interactivity 979 -> 999.\n\n* test(engine): stub yield_gil in the busy-loop accounting test's extracted scope\n\nThe test compiles EngineCore.busy_loop in a namespace of stubs for the module\nglobals it reads; the loop now also calls yield_gil.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: yifehuan <yifehuan@amd.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
