          "id": "c6bfb0ad280ee23e5edb2bda78bf8c0323093eef",
          "message": "[P/D] PP stages push their Mooncake Store load terminals to the head (#3875)\n\nOn a PP prefill with the Mooncake Store offload, a stage's finished load\nwaited for its engine core's next poll between forwards, then for the\nhead's next poll and schedule(). A request loaded on every stage stayed\nunschedulable meanwhile.\n\nWhere PP runs on the Mooncake Store with one rank a stage (TP and PCP 1,\n`stages_push_load_terminals`), each stage's load thread sends its load's\nterminal to the head's kv_status socket as the load lands\n(`PPKVStatusPusher`), and the head polls KV status after each launch that\nleaves room, so a newly loaded request joins the step's next schedule().\n\n- The send never waits: when the head's pipe is full, the terminal stays\n  for the stage's own poll.\n- A load that raises still reports its failure through the stage's poll\n  (`_guard`), not the push.\n- `PPKVAggregator` is unchanged: a load is promoted or failed only once\n  every stage reported, the head's own stage 0 included.\n- Stages with more than one rank and other offload connectors keep the\n  poll.\n\nTests: which deployments push, and that `PPEngineCoreProc.__init__` takes\nthat choice; the head polling between launches; a runner's push reaching\nthe head socket, and a full pipe refusing it without waiting; the Store\nworker's terminals through the pusher, a refused one going to the poll,\nand the pusher's open / close through `register_kv_caches` and `close()`.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-27T14:46:30+08:00",
